The Tigers have kept a generally low profile through the off-season, preferring to diligently build on their surge through the second half of last season, culminating in an elimination final against Port Adelaide. While the Tigers were mauled that day on the Adelaide Oval, an earlier change in game style to a more direct route to goal has given supporters a belief they can again be a legitimate finals aspirant this year.
They will need the four players considered elite under Champion Data's rankings – Brett Deledio, Jack Riewoldt, Shane Edwards and Alex Rance – to again excel.
