Somewhat surprisingly, skipper Trent Cotchin fell into the above-average category. In a season when he changed his leadership style, becoming more demanding of teammates, he was pivotal in the Tigers' resurgence after they had won just three of their first 13 matches.
He was able to be more damaging forward of centre from round 15, winning 52 per cent of his possessions in this attacking region in the final 10 matches, up from 43 per cent during a miserable opening few months.
