Steve Rannazzisi is best known as Kevin McArthur on The League, but the actor is also a practiced stand-up comedian. His first-ever one-hour standup special, Steve Rannazzisi: Manchild, airing Saturday on Comedy Central, focuses largely on Rannazzisi's experience with his family and two young kids. The comedian clearly has a lot of opinions, especially when it comes to dealing with children, so we enlisted him to help guide us through the often tumultuous holiday season.
Rannazzisi, who loves the holidays, said that he actually has very little real responsibility from Thanksgiving through New Year's Eve. "My wife takes care of buying the presents and all that stuff so I get to eat," he said. "I'm the party guy. She takes care of all the logistical things and I get to have a good time during the holidays. That's why I love the holidays. I'm a shit pig during the holidays. That's like asking an eight-year-old, 'What do you think about Christmas?' I'm like, 'It's great! Mommy does everything!'"
