GIFTING THE PARTY HOST
"I like to bring a dessert. Maybe a really nice baked pie. I think people appreciate that. Also you can't go wrong with a nice red wine. Like a nice pinot and a pie? If someone brought a nice pinot noir and a pie to my house, I'd be like, 'You're welcome here forever. You can sleep over.' That's the password. You can come in my house whenever you want."
GIFTING GENERALLY
"There's usually a suggestion list that heads my way late August from my wife. There's a gentle reminder around Halloween. Unless I have an idea on my own, which I rarely do, I usually get reminded of what's appropriate and what she'd like. Sometimes I'll add to that. If you don't get a suggestion list then there are some key things. I really believe everyone should have a Netflix account. So get someone a Netflix account for the year. I'm promise you I'm not sponsored by Netflix."
DRINKING
"Moderation at work parties. I do a lot of stand-up and people get too fked up during these work parties. I've seen some really obnoxious behavior. I know it's an open bar and everybody wants to let loose, but you don't want to be the person that passes out at a work party. At a family event, you gotta drink. Drink drink drink drink drink. And then before you even finish your drink, get a new one."
TRAVELING
"People always want to get to the airport super super early with families because they think it takes forever. But people generally try to get away from you. They don't want to be around you in the lines. You have that to your advantage. You can just take your time through security and then get to your gate with like 15 minutes to spare. Run the kids out. You want to get the gate, run around, and then get on the plane. And then grin and bear it. And get an iPad. I'm not sponsored by Apple either."
IF YOU'RE SINGLE
