The agreement, according to Powell, states that the teacher's obligation ends as of the last day of school, which is almost two weeks ahead of the parade this year. He added that Bryson has a supplemental contract to work outside the contract, "but it isn't specific on what exactly to do and not to do, so she was following the association's advice."
